   $q$Ines tells her friends she is learning a lot, "the way people say they love a gift they plan to return." What does this comparison suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She is privately frustrated by her limited role there.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She plans to quit the studio before the end of the year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstated-inference"},{"text":"She is excited about the work and eager to share it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"She feels guilty for not telling her friends about Dov.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She is privately frustrated by her limited role there.$q$, $q$People who plan to return a gift only pretend to love it, so Ines's words hide disappointment about only sweeping and watching. Nothing says she plans to quit; the comparison is about her feelings, not a decision.$q$, 'draft', '4d293e7f-c0a0-577f-a6c7-324e19dd44ae')
