   $q$Which inference about Tobias is best supported by thorough evidence from the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He was a careless recorder, since his entries were less precise than his daughter's.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"He valued Hester's precision, since he kept her half degrees and wrote \"Hester's method.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"He stopped caring about the ledger after his injury and let Hester finish it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"He was upset that Hester changed his records, so he went back to whole degrees.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He valued Hester's precision, since he kept her half degrees and wrote "Hester's method."$q$, $q$After October, Tobias's ink entries use half degrees until 1903, and he labeled the change "Hester's method," showing he adopted and credited her approach. He did not return to whole degrees, and twelve years of steady entries argue against carelessness.$q$, 'draft', '159dae90-fd07-5b66-9a26-5393df1ab587')
