   $q$What does Mei's reply, "But he was out of time, and I wasn't," reveal about why she refused the draw?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She believed her position on the board was stronger than his.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She did not understand that Lorenzo had offered her a draw.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She wanted to make the game last longer for the watching crowd.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She knew she was worse on the board but counted on his low clock.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She knew she was worse on the board but counted on his low clock.$q$, $q$She answers Tunde's "You were worse" with "I know," then points to the clock, so she chose to play on because Lorenzo was nearly out of time. Her "I know" rules out the belief that her position was stronger.$q$, 'draft', '0ba977b6-b0ef-5ef9-9e77-8f888d269a25')
