   $q$Which inference about Tunde is best supported by details from both the beginning and the end of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He thinks Mei played badly and wants to reteach her the basics.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-evidence"},{"text":"He is proud of Mei and wants to play chess with her again after years apart.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He wants to throw away the old board now that Mei plays in tournaments.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"He is jealous of Mei's win and wants to prove he is still better.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He is proud of Mei and wants to play chess with her again after years apart.$q$, $q$He "had not played her since" she was nine, yet he smiles "in a way she had not seen in a while" and asks her to set up the old board after dinner. He does say she was worse, but his smile and his request show pride rather than criticism.$q$, 'draft', '0ba977b6-b0ef-5ef9-9e77-8f888d269a25')
