   $q$Which pair of details best supports the inference that Ravi was determined to log the island station correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The station was in the Pacific, and it was seven thousand miles away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"He did not wake Mrs. Ostrowski, and he sat back after logging it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weak-evidence"},{"text":"He pressed the headphones to his ears and repeated the call sign three times.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He talked too fast early on, and he wrote Ohio instead of Idaho.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-time-period"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He pressed the headphones to his ears and repeated the call sign three times.$q$, $q$Pressing the headphones to hear the faint voice and repeating the call sign "to be sure" both show care for accuracy, a contrast with his rushed first hour. The distance explains why the contact mattered, not how careful he was.$q$, 'draft', 'a6a05ab9-b449-5c56-ae70-4422edf5b9f8')
